  "summary_en": "Part 13 of the US Federal Acquisition Regulation prescribes simplified acquisition procedures for purchases up to the simplified acquisition threshold, and up to $9–15 million for commercial items. It covers micro-purchases, purchase orders, blanket purchase agreements, fast payment and documentation. It has no AI or robotics content beyond a passing drone-procurement prohibition.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Agencies must use simplified acquisition procedures for purchases up to the simplified acquisition threshold.",
   "Purchases above the micro-purchase threshold up to the simplified acquisition threshold are set aside for small businesses.",
   "Subpart 13.5 allows simplified procedures for commercial items up to $9 million ($15 million in special cases).",
   "Micro-purchases remain subject to bans on Kaspersky, covered telecoms, TikTok and drone prohibitions.",
   "Sole-source justifications and file documentation are required."
  ],
